WEBVTT

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.210
Let me just say that I have a girlfriend right now.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.600
I don't, but if I tell him I
have a girlfriend, he'll stop.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.460
You know, you're a working adult,

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.780
you might want to brush up on your lying.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.750
It's not a lie, it's the truth!

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.330
Then stop avoiding my eyes.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.830
Look me in the eyes and tell me one more time.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.050
I...really do have a girlfriend.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:30.750
Liar.

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:36.840
Please stop!

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.750
Please stop!

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:49.110
Takano!

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.350
Sto...

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.540
Onodera...

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:04.960
Hey!

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.370
Hey, Onodera!

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.630
What are you doing here?

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.630
We had some work to do.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.140
We were checking the storyboard.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.140
You can't be serious.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.530
It's two in the morning.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.400
Well, what are you doing here?

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.210
I told you I was coming.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.050
Showing up...

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.370
...is the only way to get you to keep your promise.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.870
I've come to attack.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.360
Are you stupid?

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.130
Go home.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.590
I'm coming in.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:41.730
And I'm leaving.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.660
Was he tearing into you?

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:49.990
He doesn't care if you're
a rookie or an old-hand.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.300
If you do half-assed work,
he'll get rid of you fast.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.170
Stop your teary-eye thing,
it's embarrassing.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.930
I'm not-!

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:01.300
What are you two going on about?

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.560
Excuse me.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.130
Onodera.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.850
I'll call you later.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:10.870
That's not necessary.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.570
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.570
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.110
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.110
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:04.740
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:04.740
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.540
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.540
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:15.550
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:15.550
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.380
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.380
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:23.760
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:23.760
If I reach out my hand

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.140
hajimete no kimochi

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.140
Will you understand my feelings?

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:30.520
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:30.520
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.900
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.900
I love you more and more every second

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:41.030
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:41.030
We're still far from a happy ending

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:50.000
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:50.000
But I want to make it come true

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.460
tsuzuite yuku

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.460
Our story continues

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:13.560
Why did Yokozawa come here
in the middle of the night?

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.690
And why did Takano let him in?

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:20.110
He paid too much attention to me, too.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.310
He said he came to attack.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.940
Stop thinking about it and do some work.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.540
My body aches...

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.050
The places he touched still burn...

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.480
They feel feverish.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.020
I can't...

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.500
There's no way I can get through
the storyboard like this.

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:13.850
It would be an insult to the author who worked so hard.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.750
Stop doing everything so half-assed.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.760
Come on! Concentrate!

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.160
You've got to get this done!

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.410
That's right.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.830
I decided way back.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.870
I'm not going to fall in love with Takano ever again.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:02.770
Marukawa Publishing

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.360
This is Marukuwa Publishing, Onodera speaking.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:11.600
Oh, Miss Mutou! Thank you for calling.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.120
Oh, no... I'm starting to see double...

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.400
What's wrong?

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.060
Your assistants are all down with the flu?!

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.850
One of the helpers brought the virus in?!

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.660
And are you all right?

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:24.550
Hey, hey, hey!

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.610
Where the hell is the manuscript?

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:26.950
Why isn't it here?

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:29.000
We need it right now!

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:29.000
I see, that's good to hear.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.570
Oh, no!

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.110
We should've had her come to Tokyo right away!

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.780
You're going to apply all the screentone yourself now?

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:37.960
Excuse me, but can you all be quiet for a second?!

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.320
As I'm sure you already know,

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.280
after a lot of negotiation,

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.960
the deadline at the printers is at noon today.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.470
Takano!

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.470
That's right.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.970
So time-wise it's... Yes.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:55.210
I heard that one of this month's star author's dropping off.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:55.970
Is that true?

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:59.100
If it is, you need to inform us right away!

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.870
That information needs to be reported all over!

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:04.300
That was fast! He already heard.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.230
Nothing gets by the wild horse.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:07.230
What did you say?

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:10.280
I'm very sorry,

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.430
but I'm sure I can get it done by tonight.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.980
I could be on the plane around five or six,

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.630
and can apply the screentone...

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:19.920
You can't bring knives on planes anymore.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:24.410
Could you hold for a moment?

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.510
If she gives it to me at the airport at six,

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:34.590
I'll arrive at Haneda by 8:30.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:36.940
It's cutting it close.

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:39.330
All right.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:42.300
Please keep on working.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.400
I will!

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.630
Where does that author live?

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.320
Hokkaido.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.240
Are you serious?!

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.400
You're never going to make it.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.890
You have to act fast in a situation like this,

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.580
or it'll all just fall apart!

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:55.450
Tell her it's off.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:57.980
You're right.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:07:59.370
Please!

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.970
Can we just have half of a day?

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.740
I'm going to Hokkaido right now.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.170
I'll be back by nine.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.050
I'll negotiate with the printer myself.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:09.910
Just stop.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.030
It's too late.

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:15.320
There's no way she can finish
under these conditions.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.870
Kisa, bring me the list of alternate titles.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.060
Yes, sir.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.360
One moment, please!

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.850
Miss Mutou is trying as hard as she can!

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:25.590
And that's why...

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.520
Onodera!

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.310
I tried hard. I gave it my best.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.880
That's the enthusiasm we don't need,

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.320
the sort that doesn't produce results.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.690
The more you're cornered,
the more important it is...

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:41.330
...to make your decisions based on
reality and not your personal feelings.

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.330
That's what your job as an editor is.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:48.670
But we can do this.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.480
She said she would come
meet me at the airport!

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.880
You can't even think about
taking an unfinished,

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.740
white draft without screentones.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.850
Our magazine doesn't put
out that kind of material.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.410
Tell her it's off.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:02.580
It's a waste of time.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.450
But I'm telling you that I'll go get it!

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.330
If I couldn't do it, I wouldn't say that I can!

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:13.950
Amazing confidence...

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:16.360
...when you have nothing to back it up with.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.120
Fine, go.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:24.090
Huh?

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:27.640
In the worst case, I accept full responsibility.

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:30.250
Hurry up and go!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:31.970
Yes, sir!

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:38.340
Hey, Takano, how dumb are you?

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.140
This isn't a junior high manga club.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:45.290
Don't I know it.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.300
Are you Miss Mutou?

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:41.970
Yes.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.060
I'm Onodera, from Marukawa Publishing.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.330
Oh!

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:47.430
It's nice to meet you face to face.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.040
I'm so sorry!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:51.830
I'm so sorry you had to come
all the way here for this.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:52.960
It's fine, really.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.970
But that is quite the outfit...

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:59.270
I wanted to make sure no
germ could get through.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.150
And how is the manuscript?

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:05.600
I'm very sorry. There are
still fifteen pages left to go.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.770
Can you just give me what you have done?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.020
I'll apply the photo-typeset.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:23.570
Even with the glasses, I can
see the bags under her eyes.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:25.260
She's been getting no sleep.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:29.530
Her face is red and I'm pretty
sure she has a fever.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:32.330
I guess she caught that flu.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.470
Takano says he doesn't need just
enthusiasm, but I don't know.

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.070
I mean, yes, she is somewhat...

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:44.640
...to blame for getting into this situation,

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:48.990
but it's also my fault for not
checking the schedule properly.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.420
When I see her working so hard,

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:56.770
I really want to do something
as I'm responsible for her.

00:11:58.020 --> 00:11:59.280
Am I too soft?

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:00.310
Huh?

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:01.980
Nothing!

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:09.530
But isn't it the editor's
job to protect the writer?

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.020
But then, if this manuscript gets cut,

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.380
I'm not the one who'll have to take the fall.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:18.880
That will be...

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.790
I accept full responsibility.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.050
Hurry up and go!

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.540
If one part starts slipping,

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:31.230
the effect ripples all the way to the end.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:35.410
I'm an editing nobody, so
if something goes wrong,

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:37.180
I don't even have the right
to grovel for forgiveness.

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:43.990
And yet I had to rebel against
Yokozawa and be defiant.

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:46.570
That reminds me...

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:47.930
Yes?

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:51.630
Having you correct the
storyboard was the right choice.

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:53.100
Oh, really?

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.540
Especially the pacing on this page.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:59.590
I never noticed until that was pointed out.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:04.660
These kinds of things are
so hard to notice yourself.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:06.240
I wanted to say thank you.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.440
I'm glad they helped.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:09.560
I'll try my best!

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.280
But let's get this project done.

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:13.590
Yes, sir!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:18.990
That's the part Takano corrected.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.640
I understand that I can't
expect to be perfect at this...

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.990
...from the very start.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:30.880
All I have is my useless
enthusiasm running wild,

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:33.810
churning out half-assed results.

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:38.330
Are you all right?

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:40.900
Yes.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.800
Right now, I just have to do the best I can.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:19.040
Takano, we can't wait any longer!

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.020
Please accept my apologies.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:22.760
It's certain that the manuscript...

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:24.060
...is on its way here from Haneda,

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.550
so could you wait just a little longer?

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:27.020
Time's up.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:28.190
Cut it.

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:31.050
Takano!

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.180
Just a little bit longer...

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:35.180
No!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.310
I'm sorry to keep you waiting, but I'm back!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:39.720
You're late!

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:40.850
You're too late!

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.320
I'm really sorry! There was a traffic jam!

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:44.760
The phototypesetting is done?

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:45.790
The places we pointed out?

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.180
Everything is done.

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:48.360
The final check was done?

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.050
I checked it three times!

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.310
I'll take it from here.

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:54.790
Thank you very much!

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:03.850
I am truly sorry.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:09.160
This is all because I didn't
properly supervise my author.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:13.450
Then I let my emotions run away with me,

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.400
and I caused you all a lot of trouble.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:19.850
It won't happen again.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:25.760
Well, if that's all, then I'm going back to work.

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.490
You know that the agent's
already gone home, right?

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:32.090
Ever heard of this glorious
invention called the cell phone?

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:33.990
I'll call you later.

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:35.930
Thank you!

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:41.220
He was waiting, too...

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:43.500
Well, it was his responsibility as well.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.500
He's got his pride, that's for sure.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.380
But it's fine, isn't it?

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:57.890
In the end, you got it in.

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.890
It shouldn't have happened though.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.990
Well, everyone was acting like
it was the end of the world,

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:07.370
but I wasn't so worried.

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:08.030
Really?

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:11.150
For you it's not a matter of can or can't do.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.620
Once you say you're going to do something,

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.120
you do everything to make it happen.

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:20.540
That's why I wasn't worried.

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:26.080
I've always liked that about you.

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:32.300
Good job.

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:46.310
The place where he touched me aches...

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:51.740
I don't want him to get any closer to me.

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:07.900
Come on, pull yourself together!

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:09.650
You may be working for a shojo manga publisher,

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:12.350
but you can't start simpering
like some manga maiden!

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.020
Excuse me, Yokozawa.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:19.040
I didn't know you were in here.

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:22.940
Is something wrong?

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:26.350
You've got guts to come to Marukawa.

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:27.750
Excuse me?

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.030
Did you come here knowing
Masamune was working here?

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:35.360
I'm sorry, what are you talking about?

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:40.240
Did you know it's your fault
he's all screwed up now?!

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:42.550
What?

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:44.370
My fault?

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:45.700
What the...?

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.270
What is this person talking about?

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:50.680
I'm sorry,

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.000
but I'm not sure I understand.

00:17:52.890 --> 00:17:55.220
Just don't get above yourself.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:57.890
Uh...

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:03.960
What? You're still here?

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:05.720
Yeah. No rest for the weary.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:15.530
Yokozawa calls Takano by his first name...

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.720
I'm glad this got done
without further ceremony.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:27.080
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:31.050
These are the colored proofs
for next month's comics.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.710
You know how to check them, right?

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.920
Yes. I can do it.

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:45.220
What exactly does Yokozawa know?

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:48.560
First, I have to figure out
what the relationship...

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.560
...between Yokozawa and Takano is.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:57.850
It's not like I can ask Takano about that.

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:00.390
Not that I even want to.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:05.900
So I was thinking of making you
the magazine's program director,

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.930
starting the month after next.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:12.580
Onodera, are you listening?

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:28.670
And if I did ask him, how would he answer?

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:33.280
What kind of answer am I expecting?

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:48.770
I slept so well...

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:50.600
What time is it?

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.260
Shut up and be quiet already!

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:03.810
What's going on?!

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:06.100
Why the hell are we sleeping in the same bed?!

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:10.140
Because you fell asleep in the subway!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:10.940
What?

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:13.080
I guess this is the thanks I get...

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.020
...for carrying you home
and putting you in bed!

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:16.750
Ever heard of a thank you?!

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:18.900
Do you have any idea how heavy you are?

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:21.810
What am I going to do?!

00:20:21.810 --> 00:20:23.620
I don't remember anything!

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:24.650
God damn it.

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:26.660
Is it still this early?

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:31.020
I'm just asking to make sure,

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:33.670
but we didn't do anything...weird, right?

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:36.540
Define "weird."

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:38.380
You know exactly what I'm ta...

00:20:44.920 --> 00:20:46.640
Just think that we did.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:49.310
It's not a problem if you love me, right?

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.180
I'm going home.

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:56.530
Thank you so much for taking
the trouble to bring me home.

00:20:56.530 --> 00:20:59.620
Next time though, if you'll be
so kind as to just let me be.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:03.040
Just calm down.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:04.280
There's no way anything happened.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.340
That's right! Nothing else makes sense!

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:09.680
I can't let him provoke me any further!

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:13.210
My keys...

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:28.240
I want to make this clear.

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:30.680
You seem to have some kind
of misconception about me,

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:33.220
but I haven't confessed my love to you.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:35.600
Besides, there's no way I'd
ever fall in love with you!

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:38.610
That's impossible.

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:43.050
God, this guy pisses me off!

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:46.350
This is not love, this is
not love, this is not love!

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:49.000
This is most definitely not love!

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:58.960
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:58.960
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:04.340
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:04.340
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:12.430
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:12.430
I fell in love with you

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:15.940
yuugure no kaze no nioi

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:15.940
In a sunset, filled with the scent of the wind

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:20.860
boku wa omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:20.860
When I remember your voice and your smile

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:25.780
kimi no koe sono waraikata

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:25.780
I'm instantly happy

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:30.070
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:30.070
I fell in love with you

00:22:30.370 --> 00:22:34.000
dare ni mo mada ietenai

00:22:30.370 --> 00:22:34.000
But I haven't been able to tell anyone yet

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:38.460
hitori omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:38.460
When I remember your voice and the way you talk

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:42.960
sono koe shaberi kata

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:42.960
Even though I'm alone I'll be happy

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:48.130
samishii kimochi potsuri

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:48.130
The feeling of loneliness... isolated

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:51.550
sukina kimochi kirari

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:51.550
The feeling of love... sparkling

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:57.060
futatsu kubetsu ga tsukanai boku wa

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:57.060
I'm unable to tell these two feelings apart

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:01.690
yuugure ni kokoro tsuburete ku

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:01.690
My heart is slowly crushed as the sun sets

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:06.070
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:06.070
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:10.530
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:10.530
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:14.910
asa no hikari ga afure dashitara

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:14.910
Once the morning light pours in

00:23:14.910 --> 00:23:21.000
suki to yuou yuuki motte

00:23:14.910 --> 00:23:21.000
I'll courageously say I love you

00:23:25.650 --> 00:23:26.960
Marukawa publishing glossary!

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:27.860
Today's word is storyboard.

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:29.090
The storyboard is a stage during the creation...

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:30.590
...of a manga that comes after
the plot's been decided on.

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:32.590
Its purpose is to make sure the
overall flow and composition is okay.

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:35.600
All the details, like expressions and actions,

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:36.850
are drawn in roughly.

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:38.480
For picture books, it might

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:40.060
simply be called a rough draft.
